over my vehicle again. I was quite upset with him for doing this to my account so I did previously attempt to contact him and find out how this could be resolved. I felt he was being insensitive to my situation as he was trying to say that I should be happy he even put the fees to the back of my loan and that my car was still behind due to the storage fees incurred. He insisted that he has done all he can to help but instead he has caused us immense distress in this situation. Also not only did we encounter a financial issue but once the van was finally returned to me I noticed that the car was leaking and overheating from damage to the underbed of the car. As I look further there I notice the hood latch was broken and only made to look like it was fully closed. The latch has been broken. There are also many missing parts, and new hoses that have been taken out and replaced with similar older parts from a similar vehicle including a battery that I recently bought and still had a warranty on. They rewired some parts of my starter and engine to a small battery connected to a main battery which is causing a lot of electrical issues and indicators to spawn. I can not replace my battery without the core battery so I tried to reach out to XXXX again providing him with pictures and video of the issues the car returned with. I then asked for the information they had on my car from the repairs done on my vehicle as he was reading them to me. He would go on to say that I needed to go through my insurance for repairs because neither the auction vendor nor the towing company took responsibility for any damage and claimed that they could not prove that those damages were/ were not already there. I told him I will be pursuing this matter in small claims if I have to and that this treatment is wrong, I disconnected our call and since then they have been calling me and hanging up. When I do try and answer someone I explained to them that my situation has been exacerbated by so much