8063322,2023-12-27,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to formally request that Equifax, XXXX, XXXX, ( collectively, the ( Consumer Reporting Agencies '' ) cease sharing my personal information with any third parties, including furnishers of information to credit agencies, without my express written consent. 


Statutory Basis : My request is based on the following provisions of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and other applicable regulations : 15 U.S.C. 1681 ( a ) : This section emphasizes the need for credit reporting agencies to handle consumer information with fairness, impartiality, and respect for privacy. 
15 U.S.C. 16801 : This section declares the Congressional policy that financial institutions must respect customer privacy and protect the confidentiality of nonpublic personal information.

15 U.S.C. 1681 ( b ) and 1684 ( a ) ( 2 ) : These sections limit the circumstances under which credit reports can be furnished, requiring either written consumer consent or specific legal authorization.

15 U.S.C. 1681c ( a ) ( 5 ) : This section prohibits credit reports from containing certain adverse information, including outdated criminal records.

15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( a ) ( 1 ) : This section prohibits furnishers from reporting inaccurate information to credit reporting agencies.

15 U.S.C. 1681 ( e ) : This section requires credit reporting agencies to maintain reasonable procedures to prevent violations of the FCRA.

12 C.F.R. 1016.7 : This regulation allows consumers to opt out of receiving credit reports at any time. 


Specific Concerns : Sharing of Information Without Consent : I have not provided any written or verbal consent for the Credit Reporting Agencies to share my personal information with any third party, including furnishers of information to credit agencies. 
Reporting of Adverse Item : The report contains an adverse item that is being reported again without my permission. This violates 15 U.S.C. 1681c ( a ) ( 5 ) if the item is outdated or inaccurate. 
Lack of Nondisclosure Option : I was not informed of my right to opt out of having my information shared with furnishers, as required by 15 U.S.C. 16802 ( b ) ( c ). 

